  "tagline": "Rust telemetry datalake for logs, metrics and traces on S3, queried with SQL.",
  "description": "Parseable is a lightweight, Rust-built telemetry store that writes logs, metrics, traces and events to object storage as Apache Parquet and queries them with SQL through Apache DataFusion. It ingests OpenTelemetry natively as well as plain HTTP JSON, ships its own console for search, dashboards and alerts, and keeps a local hot tier for recent data so common queries avoid round-trips to S3. The server is AGPL-3.0, and Parseable's enterprise edition and managed cloud add multi-node query, SSO and support. It suits teams that want an S3-native alternative to Elasticsearch or Loki with few moving parts.",
